# Profile entry for odrl:language over the BCP 47 slice.
#
# The sort is nom.  A registry supplies identity between its concepts and
# no relation over them, so isA, isPartOf and hasPart are rejected by the
# signature before the resource is opened.  That rejection is the sort
# doing its work, and this is the clearest case of it in the suite: the
# resource file has fifteen concept assertions and no order assertion at
# all.
#
# Grounding is membership in the slice, matched against skos:notation.  A
# composed tag such as en-US is well formed over registered subtags and
# names no concept here, so it is ungrounded and the verdict is Unknown
# with that value as the certificate.
#
# The background theory is the parties' registry-uniqueness rule.  A
# problem binding this profile without it gets Unknown where the
# declaration would have given a definite verdict, which is the withdrawal
# case.

@prefix odrl: <http://www.w3.org/ns/odrl/2/> .
@prefix vrep: <https://w3id.org/odrl-verdict-report#> .
@prefix ex:   <https://w3id.org/odrl-kb/profile/> .

ex:b-language-bcp47 a vrep:OperandBinding ;
    vrep:leftOperand      odrl:language ;
    vrep:sort             vrep:nom ;
    vrep:resource         <https://w3id.org/odrl-kb/bcp47> ;
    vrep:backgroundTheory <https://w3id.org/odrl-kb/bcp47/uniqueness> ;
    vrep:grounding        vrep:sliceMembership .
